{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-37354" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-37354" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $2$nd row, we obtain the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-2-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ -3 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-2-\\lambda )((1-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-(3)(-3)) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +2)({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +10) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-37354" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ed1e89aa50aeafedf94e75660cb5117aff44b782d1fdce0129ac6c1d42a8c669"} {"question" "q-37354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-37354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(\\lambda +2)({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +10)=0"] ["math" "(\\lambda +2)({\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda -10)=0"] ["math" "(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -3)=0"] ["math" "(\\lambda -1)^{2}(\\lambda +2)=0"] ["math" "(\\lambda -2)({\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +10)=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-37354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(\\lambda +2)({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +10)=0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-140449" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda $ of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-140449" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 6-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 6-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )(3-\\lambda )(6-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=3,$ $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=4,$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=6.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are always the entries on the main diagonal." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-140449" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ed1e89aa50aeafedf94e75660cb5117aff44b782d1fdce0129ac6c1d42a8c669"} {"question" "q-140449" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-140449" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\lambda \\in {-3,4,6}"] ["math" "\\lambda \\in {3,-2,6}"] ["math" "\\lambda \\in {3,0,6}"] ["math" "\\lambda \\in {3,4,6}"] ["math" "\\lambda \\in {3,4,9}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-140449" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\lambda \\in {3,4,6}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-37390" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 10 & 0 \\\\ -5 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -9 & 3\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-37390" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & 10 & 0 \\\\ -5 & -7-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 6 & -9 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $3$rd column, we obtain the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & 10 & 0 \\\\ -5 & -7-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 6 & -9 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & 10 \\\\ -5 & -7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )((8-\\lambda )(-7-\\lambda )-(-5)(10)) & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -6) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-37390" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ed1e89aa50aeafedf94e75660cb5117aff44b782d1fdce0129ac6c1d42a8c669"} {"question" "q-37390" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-37390" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +2)=0"] ["math" "(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +2)=0"] ["math" "(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -6)(\\lambda +1)=0"] ["math" "(\\lambda -8)(\\lambda +7)(\\lambda -3)=0"] ["math" "\\lambda (\\lambda -6)(\\lambda +7)=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-37390" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +2)=0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-36860" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-36860" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-2-\\lambda  & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1-\\lambda  & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $2$nd column, we obtain the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-2-\\lambda  & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1-\\lambda  & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-2-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )((-2-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-(-2)(-2)) & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -6) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda -2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-36860" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ed1e89aa50aeafedf94e75660cb5117aff44b782d1fdce0129ac6c1d42a8c669"} {"question" "q-36860" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-36860" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda -2)=0"] ["math" "(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +1)=0"] ["math" "(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda -2)=0"] ["math" "(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -2)=0"] ["math" "\\lambda (\\lambda -2)(\\lambda +2)=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-36860" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda -2)=0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-36845" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-36845" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-3-\\lambda  & 2 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 2-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $3$rd row, we obtain the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-3-\\lambda  & 2 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 2-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-3-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 5 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )((-3-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-2\\cdot 5) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -16) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-36845" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ed1e89aa50aeafedf94e75660cb5117aff44b782d1fdce0129ac6c1d42a8c669"} {"question" "q-36845" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-36845" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda +4)=0"] ["math" "(1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -10)=0"] ["math" "(1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -16)=0"] ["math" "(1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -4)=0"] ["math" "(1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-16)=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-36845" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -16)=0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-140450" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -4 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $P$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\lambda =0$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n- $\\lambda =-4$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n- The eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ has algebraic multiplicity $2$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-140450" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the matrix $\\,P-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nP-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 2 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -\\lambda  & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -4-\\lambda  & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(P-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nNotice that we can expand the $4\\times 4$ determinant across the $1$st column, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 2 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -\\lambda  & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -4-\\lambda  & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-\\lambda  & 0 & 7 \\\\ -3 & -4-\\lambda  & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, expanding the $3\\times 3$ determinant across the $3$rd row, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5-\\lambda )\\cdot (2-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -3 & -4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )(-\\lambda )(-4-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -5)(\\lambda -2)\\lambda (\\lambda +4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the eigenvalues of $P$ are $\\lambda =5,$ $\\lambda =2,$ $\\lambda =0,$ and $\\lambda =-4$  (all with algebraic multiplicity $1$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-140450" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ed1e89aa50aeafedf94e75660cb5117aff44b782d1fdce0129ac6c1d42a8c669"} {"question" "q-140450" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-140450" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-140450" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-37355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -9 & -18 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -10 & 0 \\\\ -18 & 18 & -36 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $P$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\lambda =-1$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n- $\\lambda =-10$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n- The eigenvalue $\\lambda =-10$ has algebraic multiplicity $3$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-37355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the matrix $\\,P-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nP-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & -9 & -18 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -10-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -10-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -18 & 18 & -36 & -4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(P-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nNotice that we can expand the $4\\times 4$ determinant across the $2$nd row, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & -9 & -18 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -10-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -10-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -18 & 18 & -36 & -4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-10-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & -18 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -10-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -18 & -36 & -4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, expanding the $3\\times 3$ determinant across the $2$nd row, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-10-\\lambda )\\cdot (-10-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & -3 \\\\ -18 & -4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-10-\\lambda )^{2}((-1-\\lambda )(-4-\\lambda )-54) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +10)^{2}({\\lambda }^{2}+5\\lambda -50) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +10)^{2}(\\lambda +10)(\\lambda -5) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +10)^{3}(\\lambda -5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the eigenvalues of $P$ are $\\lambda =-10$ (with algebraic multiplicity $3$) and $\\lambda =5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-37355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ed1e89aa50