\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}6-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -7-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (6-\\lambda )(-7-\\lambda )(6-\\lambda )(-2-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -6)^{2}(\\lambda +7)(\\lambda +2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-36843" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ed1e89aa50aeafedf94e75660cb5117aff44b782d1fdce0129ac6c1d42a8c669"} {"question" "q-36843" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"} {"question" "q-36843" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(\\lambda -6)(\\lambda +6)(\\lambda +7)(\\lambda +2)=0"] ["math" "(\\lambda -6)(\\lambda +6)(\\lambda -7)(\\lambda -2)=0"] ["math" "(\\lambda -6)(\\lambda +7)(\\lambda +2)=0"] ["math" "(\\lambda -6)^{2}(\\lambda +7)(\\lambda +2)=0"] ["math" "(\\lambda -6)^{2}(\\lambda -7)(\\lambda -2)=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f573799971842410fe5a6e974beb856ffdb8ac2f3d98fec1c7fe6e1a2cdd4ea"